{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>And I will bring them.</b> I Myself will bring them — this is a good measure for Israel, so that they will not say: since we were exiled among the nations let us do like their deeds. I do not leave them, but I raise up My prophets and bring them back beneath My wings, as it says (Ezekiel 20), ״וְהָעֹלָה עַל רוּחֲכֶם הָיוֹ לֹא תִהְיֶה״ etc. ״חַי אָנִי … אִם לֹא בְּיָד חֲזָקָה״ etc. (Sifra)." "<b>or then they will humble themselves.</b> Like ״אוֹ נוֹדַע כִּי שׁוֹר נַגָּח הוּא״ (Exodus 21) — if then they humble themselves. Another interpretation: perhaps — perhaps then their heart will humble itself etc." "<b>and then they will accept their punishment.</b> They will atone for their sin through their suffering."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:51.868606611Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}